ok - absent key is off: one stderr line, exit 0, no network call
ok - TYPESAFE_API_KEY= in .env activates the tool; environment and config overrides work
ok - clear: one rule Choice request, key on the fd header only, spendPriority argmax over every candidate
ok - OpenRouter clear uses the same output contract and keeps its key out of argv and child environments
ok - OpenRouter ambiguous, malformed, HTTP, and missing-model paths are handled
ok - mapping: a declared macos-keychain service and optional account become the lookup, and the key rides the fd header
ok - precedence: environment, then .env, then the declared source, which is read only when needed
ok - provider isolation: each provider reads only its own declared service, and a declaration never selects a provider
ok - effective-home isolation: only the effective config directory's declaration is consulted
ok - failure distinctions: off, a configuration error, and an unavailable source each read differently and send nothing
ok - secret containment: the declared key is on no argv, in no output, environment, or file, and only on the fd header
ok - capability probe: supported or unsupported, with no declaration read and no credential tool run
ok - with no provider set, other providers' settings leave the original off line unchanged
ok - systemone posts the unchanged request to its base URL with an optional fd-3 key
ok - systemone configuration errors, never-send base URL, partial response, and transport failure are handled
